1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,664
Teacher midterm practice, question 25.

2
00:00:04,284 --> 00:00:08,429
True or false: the atomic packing factor is zero point seven

3
00:00:08,429 --> 00:00:13,481
four for F C C, and lower, zero point six eight, for B C C.

4
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:19,345
F C C has four atoms per cell, and a equals two root two R.

5
00:00:19,345 --> 00:00:21,725
That gives zero point seven four.

6
00:00:22,346 --> 00:00:26,887
B C C has two atoms per cell, and a equals four R over root three.

7
00:00:26,887 --> 00:00:29,187
That gives zero point six eight.

8
00:00:30,787 --> 00:00:33,520
Both values are right, so the answer is A: true.

9
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:35,806
Do not swap them.

10
00:00:35,806 --> 00:00:40,997
F C C and H C P are the close packed structures, at zero point seven four.
